{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=heat+shield&media_type=image&year_start=1962&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-04-18T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-41851 (1966) --- High angle view of Spacecraft 012 Command Module, looking toward -Z axis, during preparation for installation of the crew compartment heat shield, showing mechanics working on aft bay.","keywords":["APOLLO 1 FLIGHT","APOLLO PROJECT","APOLLO SPACECRAFT","COMMAND MODULES","CONTRACTORS","FACILITIES","INSTILLATION","INSTRUMENTATION","SHIELDING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-41851","title":"SPACECRAFT (S/C)-012 - COMMAND MODULE (CM) - HEAT SHIELD INSTALLATION"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/S66-41851~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":247000,"height":1057},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/S66-41851~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":76000,"height":528},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/S66-41851~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":76000,"height":528},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/S66-41851~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":480000,"height":1585},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41851/S66-41851~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1963-09-06T00:00:00Z","description":"S63-16250 (1963) --- Workman cleaning metal framed heat shield to be used on Mercury spacecraft. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S63-16250","title":"McDonnell- Gemini"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/S63-16250~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":224000,"height":1004},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/S63-16250~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":60000,"height":502},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/S63-16250~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":60000,"height":502},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/S63-16250~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":492000,"height":1507},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S63-16250/S63-16250~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-04-18T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-41852 (1966) --- Spacecraft 012 looking toward -Y axis during installation of heat shield. Note uprighting system compressor in aft bay, at right, and Reaction Control System (RCS) valve module panel, center of photo.","keywords":["APOLLO 1 FLIGHT","APOLLO PROJECT","APOLLO SPACECRAFT","COMMAND MODULES","CONTRACTORS","FACILITIES","INSTILLATION","INSTRUMENTATION","SHIELDING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-41852","title":"COMPRESSOR - UPRIGHTING SYSTEM - APOLLO MANUFACTURING - SPACECRAFT (S/C)-102 COMMAND MODULE (CM) - NORTH AMERICAN AVIATION (NAA), CA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/S66-41852~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":176000,"height":1042},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/S66-41852~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":54000,"height":521},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/S66-41852~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":54000,"height":521},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/S66-41852~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":360000,"height":1564},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-41852/S66-41852~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/collection.json","data":[{"center":"ARC","date_created":"1964-08-14T00:00:00Z","description":"Aerial view of Gasdynamics facility in 1964 and the 20 inch helium tunnel Part of the Thermal Protection Laboratory used to research materials for heat shield applications and for aerodynamic heating and materials studies of vehicles in planetary atmospheres.  This laboratory is comprised of five separate facilities: an Aerodynamic Heating Tunnel,  a Heat Transfer Tunnel, two Supersonic Turbulent Ducts, and a High-Power CO2 Gasdynamic Laser. All these facilities are driven by arc-heaters, with the exception of the large, combustion-type laser.  The arc-heated facilities are powered by a 20 Megawatt DC power supply. Their effluent gas stream (test gases; Air, N2, He, CO2 and mixtures; flow rates from 0.05 to 5.0 lbs/sec) discharges into a five-stage stream-ejector-driven vacuum system. The vacuum system and power supply are common to the test faciities in building N-238. All of the facilities have high pressure water available at flow rates up to 4, 000 gals/min. The data obtained from these facilities are recorded on magnetic tape or oscillographs. All forms of data can be handled whether from thermo-couples, pressure cells, pyrometers, or radiometers, etc. in addition, closed circuit T. V. monitors and various film cameras are available. (operational since 1962)","keywords":["Aerial"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"ARC-1964-A-33038-22","title":"ARC-1964-A-33038-22"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/ARC-1964-A-33038-22~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":161000,"height":853},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/ARC-1964-A-33038-22~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":426},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/ARC-1964-A-33038-22~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":426},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/ARC-1964-A-33038-22~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":329000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/ARC-1964-A-33038-22/ARC-1964-A-33038-22~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-22930/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-02-26T00:00:00Z","description":"A/S 201 was launched from the Kennedy Space Center Launch Complex 34 at 11:12 a.m., 02/26/1966. The instrumented Apollo Command and Service Module, and, a spacecraft Lunar Excursion Module Adapter, was successfully launched on the unmanned suborbital mission by the Saturn 1B to check spacecraft launch vehicle mechanical compatibility and to test the spacecraft heat shield in a high-velocity re-entry mode.     CAPE KENNEDY, FL","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-22930","title":"APOLLO/SATURN (A/S) 201 - LAUNCH - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-22930/S66-22930~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":172,"size":9400,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-22930/S66-22930~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":172,"size":9400,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-22930/S66-22930~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/collection.json","data":[{"center":"MSFC","date_created":"1966-08-01T00:00:00Z","description":"AS-202, the second Saturn IB launch vehicle developed by the Marshall Space Flight Center, lifts off from Cape Canaveral, Florida, August 25, 1966. Primary mission objectives included the confirmation of projected launch loads, demonstration of spacecraft component separation, and verification of heat shield adequacy at high reentry rates. In all, nine Saturn IB flights were made, ending with the Apollo-Soyuz Test Project (ASTP) in July 1975. ","keywords":["Saturn IB","AS-202"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"6644543","title":"Saturn Apollo Program"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/6644543~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":868,"size":70000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/6644543~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":434,"size":24000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/6644543~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":434,"size":24000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/6644543~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1303,"size":136000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/6644543/6644543~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":6}}}